To interface with an external data storage service, the `CryptoManager` class uses a custom binary format for database interaction. This approach minimizes overhead in data conversion and transmission while ensuring efficient memory usage. The library also includes retry logic and error handling strategies to account for potential network latency and service outages.

The design of the `CryptoManager` class prioritizes thread safety, leveraging asynchronous processing for I/O-bound operations. This approach helps maintain system responsiveness under high-load conditions while ensuring efficient memory usage and robust data integrity checks using HMAC-SHA256. The library also supports future extensions with minimal disruption by separating the cryptographic primitives from the key management algorithms.

