This function uses a lock-free data structure to minimize contention and ensure optimal performance. It also supports asynchronous operations, allowing for non-blocking updates and retrievals of the list contents. The function includes a garbage collection mechanism to periodically clean up unused structures to prevent memory leaks, balancing the trade-off between garbage collection frequency and system responsiveness. Finally, it provides detailed metrics and logging to monitor the health and performance of the linked list under various load conditions."]

