# Memory Allocation and Deallocation

### Dynamic Memory Allocation Strategy

To optimize memory allocation for the `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures, we can use a more advanced allocation strategy that minimizes fragmentation and maximizes cache locality. We can use a combination of `mmap()` and `munmap()` to allocate and deallocate memory in large chunks. This approach ensures that the allocated memory is contiguous, reducing the overhead of memory fragmentation.
```c
#include <sys/mman.h>
#define PACKET_SIZE sizeof(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T)
#define MAX_PACKETS 10000

typedef struct {
    NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *packets;
    int num_packets;
} packet_container_t;

void allocate_memory(packet_container_t *container, size_t bytes) {
    void *addr = mmap(NULL, bytes, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, MAP_PRIVATE | MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0);
    if (addr == MAP_FAILED) {
        perror("mmap");
        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
    }
    container->packets = addr;
    container->num_packets = bytes / PACKET_SIZE;
}

void deallocate_memory(packet_container_t *container) {
    int ret = munmap(container->packets, container->num_packets * PACKET_SIZE);
    if (ret == -1) {
        perror("munmap");
        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
    }
}
```
### Thread-Safe Deallocation Function

To ensure thread-safe operations in a multi-threaded environment, we can use a mutex to protect the deallocation function. This ensures that only one thread can access the memory at a time and avoids race conditions or other synchronization issues.
```c
#include <pthread.h>

static pthread_mutex_t dealloc_lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

void deallocate_memory(packet_container_t *container) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&dealloc_lock);
    int ret = munmap(container->packets, container->num_packets * PACKET_SIZE);
    if (ret == -1) {
        perror("munmap");
        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&dealloc_lock);
}
```
# Data Population

### Unique Identifiers and Random CRC Flags

To populate the `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures with unique identifiers and random CRC flags, we can use a combination of `rand()` and `time()` functions to generate random numbers and timestamps. We can also use the system's clock to determine when packets are generated, which allows us to measure the packet generation rate.
```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>

void populate_packets(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *packets, int num_packets) {
    srand(time(NULL));
    for (int i = 0; i < num_packets; ++i) {
        packets[i].header.message_id = rand();
        packets[i].crc_indication_body.crc_flag = rand() % 2;
    }
}
