### Validation Checks

To ensure that all structures are correctly initialized before processing begins, we can add validation checks to the `populate_packets()` function. We can check that each structure has a valid message ID and CRC flag value, which ensures that the data is consistent and complete.
```c
void populate_packets(NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T *packets, int num_packets) {
    srand(time(NULL));
    for (int i = 0; i < num_packets; ++i) {
        packets[i].header.message_id = rand();
        packets[i].crc_indication_body.crc_flag = rand() % 2;
        if (!is_valid_packet(&packets[i])) {
            fprintf(stderr, "Invalid packet at index %d\n", i);
            exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
        }
    }
